@startuml
title OctoPrint / Marlin M495 — PIS v2 host arming
hide footbox
actor User
participant "OctoPrint plugin" as P
participant Marlin as M
participant "Sensor wrapper" as S

User -> P : Detect Native M495
P -> P : Save plugin settings
P -> M : M118 opening query marker
P -> M : M495 Q
M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:READY:1
P -> M : M118 closing query marker
P -> M : M118 opening v2 marker
P -> M : M495 Q2
M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:READY:2
P -> M : M118 closing v2 marker
P -> P : Save support and select Native M495
note over P,M
  Q asks for v1; Q2 explicitly negotiates v2.
  Q1 is not an accepted token.
  Queries cannot home or start a test.
end note

User -> P : Calibrate X or Y
P -> M : M495 X F20 T60 O20 A40 I12345678 S W
M -> M : Home axes
M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:HOMED:12345678:<millis>
M -> M : Position and prepare generator
M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:ARMED_WAIT:12345678
note right of M
  Generator remains off.
  30-second ARM timeout starts now.
  Command processing remains available;
  conflicting motion/settings are rejected.
end note
P -> S : Start capture
S --> P : Alive, new samples, increasing timestamps
P -> P : Recheck sensor health
P -> M : M495 I12345678 R
M -> M : Validate ID, port, deadline, cancellation,
M -> M : operational/trusted-axis and prepared state
M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:ARM_ACK:12345678
M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:START:12345678:X:20.00:60.00
M -> M : Run native excitation
S --> P : Record acceleration

alt Successful sweep
  M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:COMPLETE:12345678
  note right of M : All native movement and pending FT step bits drained
  P -> S : Capture 0.5 s tail, then Q
  S --> P : Successful EOF; metadata when available
  P -> P : Verify settings, analyze and show results
else Sensor failure or user cancellation
  P -> M : M496
  P -> M : M118 cancellation queue fence
  M --> P : echo:PIS:RT:ABORTED:<id> or ERROR:<id>:<reason>
  M --> P : Cancellation fence received
  P -> S : Stop capture
  P -> P : Verify cleanup or require recovery
end

note over P,S
  Host, firmware and sensor clocks are independent.
  Missing/late ARM cannot start excitation.
  Sensor failure after ARM requires cancellation even before START is received.
  No automatic movement retries.
end note
@enduml
